2026-08-28 mitochondrial assembly trace

Input
- data/inputs/collection_of_pacbio_data/err13917223/err13917223.fastqsanger.gz
- PacBio HiFi FASTQ: 1,318,768 reads; 14,880,429,452 bases; read N50 14,547 bp; 35.68% GC; no N bases.

Targeting and assembly
- Read GC/length profiling revealed a distinct mitochondrial population near 15.46 kb and 18.3% GC.
- Selected 1,606 reads (21,297,766 bases) with length >=8 kb and GC 17.5-19.5%.
- Flye 2.9.6 assembled a single tandemized draft from a controlled 120-read (~112x) subset. Self-alignment established a one-cycle draft period of 15,445 bp.
- Mapped all 1,606 candidate reads with minimap2 2.31 (map-hifi) and generated a HiFi-aware samtools 1.24 consensus.
- Circular rotation exposed and removed two unsupported draft-boundary bases. The resulting cycle is 15,448 bp.
- A further rotated, boundary-spanning consensus pass was identical to the prior 15,448 bp sequence modulo an exact 7,724 bp circular rotation.

Validation
- Candidate-read depth over the selected circular cycle: mean 1,043.8x, minimum 542x, maximum 1,333x; circular seam depth 1,333x.
- Haploid bcftools 1.24 call against the polished cycle: 0 residual variants.
- Unfiltered-input scan: 3,698 reads aligned over >=1 kb; 748 reads aligned over >=10 kb at >=99.5% identity.
- Sequence is 15,448 bp, 18.30% GC, A/C/G/T only, and has no long off-diagonal self-alignment (no retained whole-genome duplication).
- Prodigal genetic-code-5 scan of a doubled circle recovered the expected compact, bidirectional mitochondrial ORF structure, including complete ORFs of 48-537 aa.

Deliverable
- final_answer/mitogenome.fasta.gz
- One non-empty FASTA record: Agrius_convolvuli_mitogenome
